    - `week5_app_reviews_questions.ipynb`
    - `week5_merge_demo.ipynb`
    - `week5_pandas_demo.ipynb`
- When files/folders are added/renamed/moved, update this section in the same change/commit so the rules stay accurate.

General
- Prefer small, readable changes that a beginner can understand.
- Keep scripts runnable from the command line on macOS with Python 3.
- Use clear variable names and consistent formatting (PEP 8-ish).
- Do not add large dependencies unless necessary; if you do, add/update `requirements.txt`.
- Avoid committing OS/editor noise (e.g., `.DS_Store`).

Paths and folders
- This repo includes folders with spaces in names (e.g., `HCDE 530 Week 2 Project/`).
  - In shell commands, always quote paths with spaces using double quotes.
  - In Python, prefer `pathlib.Path` over hardcoded working-directory assumptions when practical.

Working with CSV data
- Assume UTF-8 (`encoding="utf-8"`) when reading/writing text.
- Use `csv.DictReader`/`csv.DictWriter` for clarity.
- Validate expected headers (`participant_id`, `role`, `response`) when building new scripts.

Dashboards / HTML
- Prefer a single self-contained HTML file when requested (no build step).
- If fetching local files (like CSV), document that the user should serve via `python3 -m http.server`
  instead of opening via `file://` (CORS/security restrictions).
- Keep UI simple, accessible (semantic elements, labels for inputs), and responsive.

Git / GitHub hygiene
- Don’t commit secrets or personal tokens.
- If adding generated outputs, consider a `.gitignore` entry rather than committing them.
